"https://api.github.com/users/omarbenhamid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/omarbenhamid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/omarbenhamid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/omarbenhamid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/omarbenhamid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/omarbenhamid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/omarbenhamid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-10T10:04:08Z","updated_at":"2025-08-10T10:04:08Z","body":"Well to give you an opinion on the topic : \r\n- There two requests that live in parallel : the Django Request made by the MCP Client to the MCP Server, and the \"Fake\" DRF request which is transmitted with the view. The two have to be isolated and that's the reason why the DRF Request Wrapper exists: to fake a request to DRF without giving access to the MCP Request from client to server.\r\n\r\nI don't have enough expertise on DRF internal to judge but I noticed that many issues are solved by giving somehow access to the original request, so maybe we should go this way. I appreciate about this MR that it uses `APIRequestFactory` which is test class, and that's an issue, but it is maintained by DRF team as DRF evolves and then keep request preparation right so I would tend to merge it.\r\n\r\n@Artui \r\n> But I can keep using the older version for now\r\nWe should try not to accept regression, so if you have time to give it a try and provide some stacktrace or more insight to make this more robust, that would be perfect.\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/comments/3172518518/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/comments/3172681532","html_url":"https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server/pull/40#issuecomment-3172681532","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/40","id":3172681532,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOns7hc69G0c8","user":{"login":"Artui","id":15174053,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTc0MDUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15174053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui","html_url":"https://github.com/Artui","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artui/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-10T14:42:04Z","updated_at":"2025-08-10T14:42:04Z","body":"> @Artui what use case would this break? If you share more info I can try and figure out a solution that continues to support it, while fixing the 2 issues.\r\n\r\nI was attempting to fix the issue of having some arbitrary metadata fields on a django `request` object passed into MCP tools. Our views depend on some `request.<field_name>` properties being there, but because of how the tool wrapper is built - this call here actually will \"reset\" the WSGI request that is passed into MCP view\r\n<img width=\"1094\" height=\"281\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b74ecbeb-f362-4aef-85ea-30752b257ef3\" />\r\n\r\nHere's a simplistic diagram that explains the issue\r\n<img width=\"748\" height=\"818\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fe2cb699-8f1f-4481-92c5-37d0655c9c95\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/comments/3172681532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/comments/3177360273","html_url":"https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server/pull/40#issuecomment-3177360273","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/40","id":3177360273,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOns7hc69YquR","user":{"login":"zacharypodbela","id":8572738,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NzI3Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8572738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela","html_url":"https://github.com/zacharypodbela","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zacharypodbela/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-12T01:07:49Z","updated_at":"2025-08-12T01:07:49Z","body":"Ah that makes sense.\r\n\r\nIn your diagram you said \"without data from middleware\" -- Can you share more details on what data the middleware adds when an API call comes in that is missing when 